# Canonical identities for git log / shortlog / blame.
#
# This comment used to say "All 4 commits here are authored as jim.galasyn@hotmail.com"
# and "no commit in this repo uses jim.galasyn@confluent.io." Both are now false: the
# repo has 20 commits as of 2026-08-01, and `337084c` — the squash-merge of PR #1,
# 2026-07-27, the commit that added this very file — is authored
# jim.galasyn@confluent.io.
#
# How it got there, since nothing local was committed with the work identity: GitHub
# squash-merge re-attributed it to the account's PUBLIC email, which is the work address,
# instead of to the branch commit's author. Confirmed 2026-08-01 in two sibling repos by
# comparing pre-squash branch commits with the squashed result — exoclimate #1 and
# proc-warden #11 were both branch-authored hotmail and both landed confluent.io. This
# repo's #1 was merged 13 seconds after exoclimate's, and matches.
#
# It is INTERMITTENT: five same-era squash merges kept the branch author, two of them
# within seconds of a re-attributed one. The trigger is undetermined, and two
# explanations are now ruled out (checked 2026-08-01 with the `user:email` scope): the
# account did not change — `gh api user/emails` reports jim.galasyn@confluent.io still
# PRIMARY, verified and public — and the merge path leaves no trace, all seven
# 07-27-era squash commits carrying committer `GitHub <noreply@github.com>` with a
# valid signature. So the
# confluent.io mapping below is CORRECTIVE, not defensive — it rewrites a real commit,
# and the mechanism can fire again on any future PR.
#
# Mapped rather than rewritten: `337084c` is pushed, and rewriting would change every SHA
# from it forward and break existing clones.
#
# The author name also appears as both "Jim" (5 commits) and "Jim Galasyn" (15); both map
# to one canonical form.
#
# Counts are a snapshot including this commit; recompute after the fact with
#   git log --format='%an <%ae>' | sort | uniq -c
#
# Format: Proper Name <proper@email> <commit@email>

Jim Galasyn <jim.galasyn@hotmail.com> <jim.galasyn@hotmail.com>
Jim Galasyn <jim.galasyn@hotmail.com> <jim.galasyn@confluent.io>
